**Proof.** Set up coordinates with $D$ at the origin and $BC$ along the $x$-axis. Since $D$ is the midpoint of $BC$, write $B=(-1,0)$, $C=(1,0)$ (scaling is harmless), and let $A=(u,v)$ with $v>0$. Put $r=|DA|=\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}$, so $r^{2}=u^{2}+v^{2}$.

The direction of $AD$ is $(u,v)$.

**Finding $E$.** In $\triangle ADB$ the internal bisector of $\angle ADB$ at $D$ has direction equal to the sum of the unit vectors along $DA$ and $DB$:
$$\frac{(u,v)}{r}+(-1,0)=\left(\frac{u}{r}-1,\;\frac{v}{r}\right).$$
The circumcircle of $A,D,B$ has equation $x^{2}+y^{2}+x-\dfrac{r^{2}+u}{v}\,y=0$ (using $D=(0,0)\Rightarrow$ no constant term, $B=(-1,0)\Rightarrow$ coefficient of $x$ equals $1$, and $A=(u,v)$ to fix the $y$-coefficient).

Parametrize the bisector ray by $(x,y)=t\bigl(\frac{u}{r}-1,\frac{v}{r}\bigr)$. Substituting into the circle and factoring out the root $t=0$ (the point $D$) gives the second intersection
$$t=\frac{r(r+1)}{2(r-u)}.$$
Hence
$$E=\Bigl(-\frac{r+1}{2},\;\frac{v(r+1)}{2(r-u)}\Bigr).$$

**Finding $F$.** Similarly, in $\triangle ADC$ the bisector of $\angle ADC$ at $D$ has direction
$$\frac{(u,v)}{r}+(1,0)=\left(\frac{u}{r}+1,\;\frac{v}{r}\right).$$
The circumcircle of $A,D,C$ has equation $x^{2}+y^{2}-x+\dfrac{u-r^{2}}{v}\,y=0$. Parametrizing the bisector ray by $(x,y)=s\bigl(\frac{u}{r}+1,\frac{v}{r}\bigr)$ and solving for the nonzero root yields
$$s=\frac{r(r+1)}{2(r+u)},$$
so
$$F=\Bigl(\frac{r+1}{2},\;\frac{v(r+1)}{2(r+u)}\Bigr).$$

**Direction of $EF$.** We compute
$$\overrightarrow{EF}=F-E=\left(r+1,\;\frac{v(r+1)}{2}\Bigl(\frac{1}{r+u}-\frac{1}{r-u}\Bigr)\right).$$
The $y$-component simplifies as
$$\frac{v(r+1)}{2}\cdot\frac{(r-u)-(r+u)}{(r+u)(r-u)}=\frac{v(r+1)}{2}\cdot\frac{-2u}{r^{2}-u^{2}}=-\frac{v(r+1)u}{r^{2}-u^{2}}.$$
Since $r^{2}-u^{2}=v^{2}$, this becomes $-\dfrac{(r+1)u}{v}$. Thus
$$\overrightarrow{EF}=(r+1)\left(1,\;-\frac{u}{v}\right)=\frac{r+1}{v}\,(v,\,-u).$$

**Perpendicularity.** Taking the dot product with $\overrightarrow{AD}=(u,v)$,
$$\overrightarrow{EF}\cdot\overrightarrow{AD}=\frac{r+1}{v}\bigl(v\cdot u+(-u)\cdot v\bigr)=\frac{r+1}{v}(uv-uv)=0.$$

Therefore $EF\perp AD$. $\blacksquare$

